+Extend the existing Rider instruction and adapter contract, and correct deep-review CLI metadata so it reports the identity of the invocation that produced the accepted packet. Carry reasoning effort separately from model identity through each supported CLI selector and worker observation. Add caller-level checks for effort, alias resolution, preflight cost, history attribution, consultation and result admission, telemetry, retry attribution, claim races, and both published schemas. Centralize route selection in Rider's keyed dispatch procedure and keep the provider reference responsible for installed-host capability facts. Reconcile earlier implementation attempts against each assertion below. Shark retains prompt assembly and workflow authority. This repair reuses the existing semantic outcome and dispatch routes. It adds a bounded `rework_outcomes` map for explicitly configured child rework, and keeps the ordinary `shark run` dispatch interface unchanged. Its structured gates share the protected writer and must still complete under a live lease. [E34-F01 decisions and implementation addendum](../E34-prompt-and-skill-improvements/E34-F01-harness-aware-prompt-rendering/decisions.md) · [E38 dispatch and ownership decisions](../E38-shark-attack-team-orchestration/architecture.md)
