+## F1. A compact change-card key can remove the other card’s link
+
+Repair step 5 requires preserving exact-key lookup order. For input `C001`, the shipped repository tries `CC-001` first. Only a genuine miss permits the second lookup for the stored spelling `C001`. The database permits both stored keys. Owner `jwwelbor` merged this lookup behavior in PR #118. Row 13 checks a canonical key and its slug, with one card in the fixture. The existing repository alias tests also seed just the canonical card. Reversing the two exact lookups yields the same results in those cases. [Shipped lookup](https://github.com/jwwelbor/shark-task-manager/blob/c0a66d2fe9295107527a2c00f80933dabaedbca6/internal/repository/changecard/repository.go#L94-L130) · [Owner merge](https://github.com/jwwelbor/shark-task-manager/pull/118) · [Existing alias tests](../../../internal/repository/changecard/repository_test.go#L115)
+
+I built the CLI from the shipped B079 tree and a separate executable with only the two exact lookup keys exchanged through a temporary Go build overlay. Both registered commands received `related-docs delete "shared title" --change=C001 --json`. Each card held a different document with that title. I read the surviving associations over a fresh SQLite connection after each process.
+
+| Starting fixture | Shipped executable | Reversed lookup |
+|---|---|---|
+| Only canonical card 21 with document 121 | Exit 0, link removed | Same |
+| Only compact-key card 22 with document 122 | Exit 0, link removed | Same |
+| Both cards | Exit 0, retained only (22,122) | Exit 0, retained only (21,121) |
+| Both cards, canonical card has an unreadable NULL priority | Exit 1 with the scan cause, both links retained | Exit 0, removed (22,122) |
+
+Both executables emitted the same success JSON on the healthy collision. The two existing repository tests for ordinary and slugged change-card aliases passed against the reversed lookup. The shipped exit 1 on a scan failure is historical evidence. The approved CLI error contract requires exit 2 for the repair.
+
+**Required assertion.** Extend row 13 with the compact selector and both stored spellings. Assert the exact survivor after success, successful lookup of the compact-only record, and exit 2 with the scan cause and both links preserved when the canonical record is unreadable. This catches reversed precedence, loss of compatibility fallback, and fallback past an operational failure.
+
+## F2. A mismatched tech-debt key and slug can select a real parent
+
+The shipped tech-debt repository requires the numeric key and supplied slug to match the same record. Row 6 exercises matching keys, valid padding, a missing TD and operational failures. Its reused B079 contracts combine a known matching slug or an absent numeric key with the registered command. Those cases cannot distinguish a fallback that checks only the key or only the slug. Row 13 has corresponding negative controls for change cards, whose command uses a different repository. [Shipped tech-debt lookup](https://github.com/jwwelbor/shark-task-manager/blob/c0a66d2fe9295107527a2c00f80933dabaedbca6/internal/repository/techdebt/repository.go#L122-L151) · [B079 compiled contracts](https://github.com/jwwelbor/shark-task-manager/blob/c0a66d2fe9295107527a2c00f80933dabaedbca6/tests/contracts/b079_research_cli_test.go#L127-L156)
+
+I seeded one item with key `TD-001`, slug `fixture` and document 131. I restored its link before each invocation. The two comparison builds each omitted one comparison from the shipped slug query. Every case used the registered `--tech-debt` delete and an independent SQL read after process exit.
+
+| Selector | Shipped executable | Key-only lookup | Slug-only lookup |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `TD-001-fixture` | 0, removed | 0, removed | 0, removed |
+| `TD-999` | 1, retained | 1, retained | 1, retained |
+| `TD-001-stale` | 1, retained | **0, removed** | 1, retained |
+| `TD-999-fixture` | 1, retained | 1, retained | **0, removed** |
+
+**Required assertion.** Extend row 6 with both mismatches. Each must return exit 1, identify the supplied key, suppress confirmation and preserve the exact association. Keep the matching pair as the successful control and the failed scan on a matching pair as the exit-2 control. This applies B079’s parent-scoped deletion decision to the repository that step 5 changes. [Owner-merged B079](https://github.com/jwwelbor/shark-task-manager/pull/285)
