+## Review of the coverage index
+
+| Row | What would make the proposed assertion fail |
+|---|---|
+| 1. Selection | Choosing the first explicit flag accepts a mixed valid/empty pair. The command must reject either order before service access. Malformed, blank and padded TD inputs also distinguish validation from normalization. |
+| 2. Dispatch and output | Wrong dispatch changes the stored association. Wrong formatting changes the JSON parent or exact human line. In flag order the labels are epic, feature, task, bug, change-card, question and tech-debt. The two hyphenated labels map to stored types `change` and `tech_debt`, respectively. |
