+| 10. Database acquisition | A panic can exit 2. Requiring the handler’s original cause, zero subsequent calls, structured JSON or human error and no stack dump distinguishes it on all seven routes. |
+| 11. Service configuration | Each of six independently implemented wrappers must return `writable document repository not configured` before storage. Question has a separate direct-service assertion. |
+| 12. Rejected write | Counting the operation and key across the entire diagnostic catches duplicated wrappers even when a narrower substring occurs once. All seven routes require the cause, exit 2 and intact associations. |
+| 13. Change-card lookup | Numeric and slugged reads of an unreadable card must retain the scan cause and exit 2. An absent card or wrong slug must exit 1. This addresses revision 3 F1. The shipped-command probe independently reproduced the slugged scan being reported as missing. F1 above concerns the earlier exact-key choice. |
+| 14. Argument checks | Exact errors for invalid type, zero ID and negative ID, type-first ordering, zero storage attempts, and a valid-input control detect premature transaction acquisition. This addresses revision 3 F2 at the direct repository boundary. |
+| 15. Cancellation | A cancelled call must preserve the original row and metadata and match `context.Canceled`. A live retry must remove the row. Propagation checks and synchronized cancellation after DELETE catch loss of context during verification. This addresses revision 3 F3. |
