+**Verdict — replan.** The qualified feature correction addresses the wrong-epic diagnosis. The Shark project owner has settled the shorthand policy. Four gaps in the coverage index still allow a repair to lose protected behavior. The first could allow deletion from a real feature after the supplied short slug matched no feature.
+
+**Reviewer** — Codex, independent TechLead plan reviewer, single-worker dispatch, 2026-11-20. I inspected the committed plan, source, owner records and historical findings, and compared the old and intended predicates on isolated SQLite data. Implementation review and QA remain pending.
+
+## Revision and decision authority
+
+- Document 452 identifies the revision at Git commit `47bdbbbd846a6092640c9ca810e5ec3d854af0ba`. Hashing its Git blob contents and its working file produced the digest above. Note 3556 and the actual Git parent of first fix `932dd5080aaa592e24a427ce1a999ee34603f554` independently identify **`bbf490c6ec2bd597d6f3e6e4cdd93e68ca54fa50`** as the review baseline. The merge base with the local upstream ref agrees. The parent-context B078 related-document list included research 415, prior plan 443, mutable evidence 444, independent reports 445–447/449/450 and plan 452. All 16 rows link to existing headings in 444. The earlier approval in note 3864 applies to the revision 5 bytes at their original path. [Revision 5 review](B078.plan-review-r5.md) · [Revision 6 plan](B078.repair-plan-r6.md)
+- **Feature identity.** E07-F11 stories 2.2 and 4.2, the completed end-to-end task, the published feature key formats, the shipped wrong-slug tests and the numeric task-suffix regression establish the existing lookup contract. On November 20, the user, acting as Shark project owner, accepted qualified keys, retained both unique shorthand forms, and directed that document delete require a full key before mutation on a cross-epic shorthand collision. The parent recorded that disposition in B078 decision **3952**. It resolves the earlier pending request in 3951 and the companion record. It matches the proposal in the committed plan. It establishes no tie-break between multiple epics. [User stories](../E07-enhancements/E07-F11-slug-architecture-improvement/user-stories.md) · [Feature key support](../../cli-reference/feature-commands.md#key-format-support) · [Shipped repository tests](../../../internal/repository/feature/repository_test.go)
+- **Selection, storage and exits.** E07-F05 has an empty related-document list. Its completed PRD and CLI task establish association-only deletion, idempotence on absence, confirmation and exits 0/1/2. E21-F08's delivered schema supersedes the original per-entity tables. The March 20 Architect Agent approval in T-E21-F08-003 covers repository validation even though the task itself is in development. E39-F01 adds Question. Shark parent decision 3603 supersedes the optional selector sketch and allows isolated compiled integration tests. Note 3625 retains Question error context and requires use of the actual legacy title winner. B079 notes 3572, 3606, 3611, 3622–3623 and 3802 and the owner-merged PR #285 supply the seven-route shared selector, typed kinds, whitespace handling and list diagnostics. B072's list inference and B079's catalog retrieval have separate ownership. The B079 code, reviews and QA support reuse of the document contracts at merge `c0a66d2fe9295107527a2c00f80933dabaedbca6`. [CLI task](../E07-enhancements/E07-F05-add-related-documents/tasks/T-E07-F05-003.md) · [E21 data model](../E21-entity-polymorphism-and-duplication-reduction/E21-F08-polymorphic-data-model-unification/tech/03-data-models.md) · [Question contract](../E39-question-and-decision-workflow-management/E39-F01-question-entity-and-platform-registration/spec.md) · [PR #285](https://github.com/jwwelbor/shark-task-manager/pull/285)
+- **Transaction and test ownership.** The service standard assigns multi-operation business transactions to services. Revision 5 approval 3864 covered a single repository operation that deletes and verifies one physical association for direct and service callers. The repository example in the Go rules is consistent with that narrow use. The plan keeps parent selection and title matching outside that operation. The existing isolated database API supports fixtures that corrupt rows or install triggers. Local use resolves the fixture concern. General standards wording remains with the standards owner. Neither interpretation grants a workflow exception. [Service rule](../../../.claude/rules/services/service-design.md#7-transaction-ownership) · [Go patterns](../../../.claude/rules/go/patterns.md) · [Database test helper](../../../internal/test/testdb.go)
