+
+The research diagnosis holds. At the baseline the five ordinary CLI branches discard errors, the shared service resolves titles globally and the repository accepts a zero-row delete. On the feature path the shipped qualified-text query drops the epic. Verifying the resulting association triple cannot recover the requested identity. The later trigger examples test the specified postcondition. They supply no evidence of a trigger in the historical WWGM incident.
+
+I verified the five retained code-review packet hashes in B078/3933. Keep that review attached to candidate `3a081dfcd0e1e17edc104060dea848b88fbdf873`. A1 and sweep 3949 remain open for implementation. A2–A8, C1, E1 and E2 retain their development findings. F1–F3 from that candidate report retain their fixture-isolation dispositions and D1 remains its stdout-helper nit. Those identifiers belong to the historical report. The four findings above belong to this plan revision. Earlier plan reports and historical code reviews retain their findings and owner dispositions, including the TC-067 live-probe skip. [Candidate findings](../../review/bugs/b078/code-review-20261120T023544Z-B078.md) · [Prior evidence](B078.repair-plan-evidence.md#retained-candidate-findings)
+
+**Parent handoff.** Return B078 to repair planning with the confirmed baseline and decision 3952. Link the missing controls and reusable evidence in the single index of a new committed revision and obtain independent review of its bytes. Candidate changes then require fresh code review and QA. This dispatch evaluated the plan through source inspection and isolated predicate comparisons. It made no change to the reviewed plan or implementation.
