+# B078 repair plan review — revision 7
+
+Reviewer: Codex TechLead, independent plan reviewer
+Verdict: **PASS**
+
+plan_path: docs/plan/bugs/B078.repair-plan-r7.md
+plan_sha256: sha256:5aee2057846d0be536fb92d23ba5ca8458273ce4bd22c247d306310d43f76251
+
+## Findings
+
+None. Revision 7 is approved as written. This review does not approve an implementation candidate or replace downstream code review and QA.
+
+## Baseline and authority
+
+The plan declares baseline `bbf490c6ec2bd597d6f3e6e4cdd93e68ca54fa50`. I confirmed it is the parent of first repair commit `932dd5080aaa592e24a427ce1a999ee34603f554`, and that the declared baseline commit exists. The plan file’s recomputed SHA-256 matches the identity above.
+
+Owner decision 3952 authorizes full qualified feature keys and preserves the existing `F02` / `F02-<slug>` lookup behavior for non-delete callers. For related-document delete, ambiguous shorthand must request a fully qualified key before listing or mutation. Revision 7 confines the ambiguity check to unlink, so the owner’s limited disposition is respected. Earlier cross-project tooling decisions do not alter Shark’s workflow or authorize a forced transition.
+
+## Coverage review
+
+Reviewed all 18 rows in the plan’s single coverage index against the B078 intake and research, the linked prior plan reviews and findings, decision 3952, current production callers, and applicable repository conventions.
+
+Rows 1–8 cover selector cardinality and routing, exact parent-scoped title resolution, association postconditions, error and rollback-cause preservation, tech-debt handling, WWGM evidence, and candidate-bound regression proof. Their assertions distinguish successful absence from failed deletion, catch ignored or restored writes, retain both operation and rollback errors, and preserve the document and unrelated associations.
+
+Rows 9–15 cover every association-key predicate in both delete and verification queries; database initialization; all six service configuration guards; one contextual unlink diagnostic; change-card canonical-key precedence and scan failures; argument validation before storage; and caller-context cancellation with rollback. Each row specifies a control or counterexample that would expose loss of the protected behavior.
+
