+
+Required evidence: a fake app-server returns a paginated v2 `model/list` response with synthetic identifiers, display names and descriptions; the requested pin appears on page two. Assert both production materialization paths retain the returned display name and description as dynamic metadata, and neither value nor the model identifier appears in static profiles or fixtures. Test both materialization paths against the real production materializer. Assert hidden-only pins, incomplete or malformed later pages, unsupported effort, missing catalog and ambiguous default all fail before adapter start. Bind discovery and dispatch to the same resolved executable/configuration; vary effective environment under the same executable and reject cross-identity catalog evidence. Capture catalog source, CLI version, selected metadata and digest without a synthetic secret or credential. With no Claude executable available on `PATH`, a catalog-advertised Codex route must reach the recording adapter exactly once, with exactly one Codex dispatch.
