+
+## Identity and authority
+
+I hashed the plan blob in commit e9ba8790183c59bd941d22702b2df9aa2af98fcb. The first B089 research commit f6bdba74d352831203e1e1930e0091ed0be24849 has parent 1dc22b13687efcccc675fc4ecced55266b61c882, exactly the declared review baseline. Git ancestry confirms it contains the PR #286 merge fda465cb79ee20d969c660e683834de9a8b9659b. The baseline-to-plan diff contains four B089 documents. The intervening changes to change.go since #286 concern get, update and delete.
+
+The parent project's B089 registry links research 468, architect decision 469 and plan 470. The resolved architect decision authorizes verification of the delivered fix and asks for the failing process's executable path and version on recurrence. Research 468 distinguishes the reproducing dirty binary from the unidentified original reporter binary. The B082 registry links recovery plan 391, research 414 and review 417. Recovery plan item 4 requires CLI parity with configuration preserved. E07-F42 defines canonical size and nullable storage. Its original optional-only scope predates the configured service policy explicitly preserved by the recovery plan and B082 closeout. Optional-policy behavior still applies when change is absent from size_required_for.
+
+I checked the B082 reviews and QA in the owning Shark checkout, including the separate six-angle R1 report, rounds 3–8 and notes 3559, 3615–3651 and 3805. The B082 parent accepted the tag fix in scope and dispositioned the unchanged display helper in note 3559. Note 3626 records the typed-renderer repair. Test fixture isolation, value variation, flag errors, helper extraction, test structure and cleanup findings were addressed before final R8 review on 864e3dca. QA and the merge establish historical delivery. TC-067 was skipped. The architect disposition supersedes the historical need for another implementation and grants no verification waiver. The creation path invokes local CLI, service and storage code. Provider selection, model settings and paid-call costs belong to separate workflow operations. None of the B089 obligations changes them.
+
+## Coverage index review
+
+Each of the six rows names an authority, boundary, action and assertion and links to a section of the separate mutable evidence record.
+
+1. **Delivery.** Checking merge containment, the two registrations in create.go, both handlers' shared helper and the production/configuration diff detects a missing repair or an extra B089 patch.
+2. **Unified creation.** The four required-policy CLI cases distinguish both registrations and both reported inputs. Reading integer 3 by distinct title catches a successful exit with incorrect storage. The XS/XXL DTO assertions detect constant forwarding.
+3. **Entity-first creation.** The stored 3, returned M and feature association exercise size and link propagation. The same handler assigns tags separately. See F1.
+4. **Omission and invalid values.** The nil-policy check in ChangeCardService.CreateChangeCard precedes key generation. The service assigns input.Size and the repository binds card.Size. Required rejection, optional SQL NULL and pre-service rejection of 4, XXXL and clear have distinct expected observations. For downstream evidence, identify the command for each case, carry the real config through the service accessor, and distinguish zero key-generation/service calls from zero inserted rows.
+5. **Tags and errors.** The B082 tests capture the exact tag slice for each unified registration. The shared reader has independent size and tag flag reads. The plan omits entity-first tag forwarding and the observable typed error contract described below.
+6. **Executable provenance.** Recording the resolved path and build revision in the actual failing process and comparing the same command and policy on a containing build can distinguish the two observed executable behaviors. The original report provides no binary identity. The recurrence requirement is conditional.
+
+## Open findings
+
