+**Disposition.** Use the change-card creation repair shipped in B082, PR #286. The Shark architect recorded this technical decision as resolved in [decision 469](../../council/decisions/d-b089-already-delivered-by-b082.yaml). After [independent review R1](B089.plan-review-r1.md), the architect and tech lead resolved [scope decision 472](../../council/decisions/d-b089-plan-review-scope.yaml). It retains decision 469 on size and qualifies its source-change limit for the adjacent tag path. Reuse the exact-input tests for F1 and add caller-level typed-error tests for F2. [Independent review R2](B089.plan-review-r2.md) approved revision 2 at commit `2012d34e5a52bf0a7f55a910848fb8d7d2e3b238`. Development then found that neither create handler could inject a vocabulary without opening the project database. In [decision 474](../../council/decisions/d-b089-tag-error-test-seam.yaml), the architect and developer authorized one package-local factory at the existing resolver. That decision supersedes revision 2’s tests-and-documents-only limit for this seam. A change to observable behavior still requires a failing creation-path assertion under decision 472. Revision 3 requires independent approval before implementing the seam or the caller tests.
+
+## Diagnosis and scope
